      "runs": {
        "gameplay-hglbtrtb": {
          "note": "The same stimuli fired the same solenoids at every step as on hglbtrtr, including the coin lockout's behaviour during the bonus count; lamp observations are cited from hglbtrtr only."
        },
        "gameplay-hglbtrtr": {
          "note": "Coin on public 10, credit on public 6 with the ball held on the outhole (8): the start fired 7 and 15 and raised 17 and 19. One closure at a time: slingshots 37 and 36 fired 11 and 12; thumper bumpers 40, 39 and 38 fired 9, 8 and 10; the globe saucer 24 fired 13 and lit the centre G (15). Drop targets 4, 3, 2 and 1 fired nothing; the second lit 2X (12), the third 3X (28) and the fourth 5X (44). The target saucer 32 with all four down fired 14 and 15 and lit the saucer target special (56). The centre right spinner 25 lit lamp 20. Players targets 26, 27, 28 and 29 put out lamps 10, 57, 41 and 25; the fifth (30) relit them and lit lamp 58. The dunk shot target 35 dropped 17 and lit lamp 37; the right outlane 23 raised 17 again and put 37 out. Holding 84 raised 47 and 48 and holding 82 raised 45 and 46; holding 81 or 83 changed no output. The drain fired 7 and 15. While the outhole bonus counted down, the ROM dropped the coin lockout (18) and raised it 5 times before the outhole kick, each time for a few tens of milliseconds except the last, which it held."
        },
        "solenoid-test-hglbtrtb": {
          "note": "Same pairing, cycle and published lamp and solenoid addresses as hglbtrtr. The player displays carry seven digits, and at power-up player 1 shows 090, the conversion's revision."
        },
        "solenoid-test-hglbtrtr": {
          "note": "Self-test pressed three times after a 30 s boot; the solenoid test then fires one output at a time while showing its number on every player display. Paired with the number on player 1's display 0.25 s after each pulse, in test order 1 to 13: 1->7, 2->6, 3->13, 4->14, 5->12, 6->11, 7->9, 8->8, 9->10, 10->15, 11->18, 12->19, 13->17. Every later pulse of the run follows the same order (3 full cycles). Before the test the power-on reset pulsed outputs 17, 18, 19, 20 together, and the ROM's start-up fired the saucer kickers (13, 14) and the drop-target reset (15) and raised the gate (17), the coin lockout (18) and the flipper relay (19).",
          "ordered_solenoid_on_sequence": [
            7,
            6,
            13,
            14,
            12,
            11,
            9,
            8,
            10,
            15,
            18,
            19,
            17
          ]
        },
        "switch-test-hglbtrtb": {
          "note": "Same as hglbtrtr: 1 to 40 shown, 41 to 48 not, and the same slingshot and bumper coils fired."
        },
        "switch-test-hglbtrtr": {
          "note": "Self-test pressed five times (the fourth press ends the cycling solenoid test, the fifth starts the switch test). Closing each of public 1 to 40 alone made the ROM show that number on the player displays; closing 41 to 48 showed nothing. The ROM fired the slingshot and thumper bumper coils for their switches in the switch test too (36->12, 37->11, 38->10, 39->8, 40->9)."
        },
        "tilt-hglbtrtr": {
          "note": "With a game running and the right flipper button held (45 and 46 up), pulsing the tilt (7) dropped 17, 19, 45 and 46 and lit lamp 61 (TILT); holding 84 afterwards raised nothing. At the drain the next ball fired 7 and 15, raised 17 and 19 and put 61 out."
        }
      },
